# Git identity: kamfur only

This repository is `https://github.com/kamfur/parktrack.git`. Always use the **kamfur** account. Never use `kamil-furtak-s4d` or `kamil@solutions4delivery.com` here.

## Required local identity

```text
user.name  = kamfur
user.email = furtakamil@gmail.com
```

Before every `git commit` or `git push`:

1. `git config --local user.name` and `user.email` must match the values above. If they do not, set them with `git config --local`.
2. `gh auth status` must show **kamfur** as the active account. If another account is active, run `gh auth switch --user kamfur`.
3. `git remote -v` origin must stay `https://github.com/kamfur/parktrack.git`.

## Examples

```text
# ❌ BAD — work account on this private repo
git config --local user.email "kamil@solutions4delivery.com"
gh auth switch --user kamil-furtak-s4d

# ✅ GOOD — kamfur for every Git and GitHub operation here
git config --local user.name "kamfur"
git config --local user.email "furtakamil@gmail.com"
gh auth switch --user kamfur
```
